The files in this directory are adapted from Blender's Cycles renderer,
https://projects.blender.org/blender/blender (mirror https://github.com/blender/blender),
at commit 052275913f65d6df3598588101345c621fd35ac8 (2026-10-25):

- intern/cycles/kernel/svm/noise.h
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2009-2010 Sony Pictures Imageworks Inc., et al. All Rights Reserved.
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2011-2022 Blender Foundation
    SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
    Adapted code from Open Shading Language.
  -> noise4d.h, noise4d.slang (perlin_4d, snoise_4d and their helpers)

- intern/cycles/util/hash.h
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2011-2022 Blender Foundation
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    hash_uint4 is Bob Jenkins' lookup3 (http://burtleburtle.net/bob/c/lookup3.c, public domain);
    hash_pcg4d_i is from "Hash Functions for GPU Rendering", JCGT 2020.
  -> noise4d.h, voronoi4d.h, noise4d.slang

- intern/cycles/kernel/svm/voronoi.h
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2011-2022 Blender Foundation
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  -> voronoi4d.h, noise4d.slang (4D voronoi_f1, Euclidean metric, distance output only)

Changes: scalar rewrite of the vector code into the subset shared by C++ and Slang, unsigned
arithmetic where Cycles relies on signed overflow, and only the functions named above.

Licensing note for the spike decision: the Perlin code is BSD-3-Clause, which is compatible with
Natron's GPL-2.0-or-later. The Voronoi code and the PCG hash wrapper are Apache-2.0, which is
compatible with GPLv3 only; distributing them in Natron would make the binaries effectively GPLv3.

This code is a spike: it is never linked into Natron.

